# titan — committed, NON-SECRET defaults. Safe to read; safe to commit.
#
# Secrets NEVER go in this file. `npm run setup` writes the generated
# AUTH_SECRET to `.env.local` (mode 0600), which stays git-ignored. That split
# is the Next.js contract: `.env` = committed defaults, `.env.local` = local
# secrets and local overrides.
#
# ── Why DATABASE_URL lives HERE and not only in .env.local (DEC-013) ─────────
# The Prisma CLI auto-loads `./.env` and `./prisma/.env`. It CANNOT read
# `.env.local` — that is a Next.js convention, not a Prisma one. So a
# `DATABASE_URL` that exists only in `.env.local` is invisible to
# `npx prisma migrate deploy`, `npm run setup` and `npm run db:migrate`, which
# fail with "Environment variable not found: DATABASE_URL" on a clean clone.
#
# The trap that follows from that, and the reason this comment is long:
# `.env.local` overrides `.env` FOR THE APP but not for the Prisma CLI. If you
# repoint DATABASE_URL in `.env.local` and leave this file alone, you will
# migrate one database and serve another, with no error to tell you.
# If you change it, change it in BOTH — or, better, only here.
#
# An explicit `DATABASE_URL=` in the environment still wins over both, which is
# how `tests/helpers/db.ts` gives each suite its own throwaway database.
#
# ── Why the value starts `../` and not `./` (TASK-016) ───────────────────────
# Prisma resolves a RELATIVE sqlite `file:` URL against the directory holding
# `schema.prisma` — i.e. `prisma/` — NOT against the repository root and NOT
# against the process cwd. `file:./data/titan.db` therefore means
# `prisma/data/titan.db`, which is where this application's database actually
# lived until TASK-016. SPEC-001 puts persistent state at `./data/titan.db`, so
# the URL has to climb out of `prisma/` to get there: `../data/titan.db`.
#
# Verify it rather than trusting the string — the string is what fooled two
# green tests for four slices:
#     DATABASE_URL="file:../data/titan.db" npx prisma migrate deploy
#     ls data/titan.db          # exists
#     ls prisma/data            # does not exist
DATABASE_URL="file:../data/titan.db"
